From 1280c8da8b3598c0f2019c63d3066edac21ad181 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 01:57:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 21/24] Render into R32Float colour attachments

macOS 26 and 27 attach a memoryless R32Float target beside the colour
target of an application window's pass. It was not renderable, so the
render-target ladder refused it (rt_memoryless_format fmt=0x37, reported
once per attachment: one on a 27.2 boot, one on a 26.6.2 boot) and the
whole multi-attachment pass went with it (mrt_request fail
slots=[17, 15, 16] on 27.2, a 507x305 window surface). Earlier research
traced the missing Terminal text on 26 and 27 to these refusals; that
link was not re-measured here.

R32_FLOAT joins render_target_bpp at four bytes, rendered natively as
R32_SFLOAT, the route RG32Float took one channel down. The CPU Load seed
writes red at its eight-bit value, the readback narrowing clamps to
[0, 1] and fills green, blue and alpha like the other single-channel
layouts, and the CPU Store converter writes through the seed expansion
as RG32Float's does. texel_to_rgba8 still has no arm for it, so a sampled
R32Float keeps its native rail. Vulkan requires R32_SFLOAT as a colour
attachment but not its blending; the attachment check added for
BGR10A2Unorm asks the host for both and refuses by name where it cannot.
The GB10 host reports both. The engine readback and seed paths already
treat a four-byte non-colour layout as one to narrow or widen.

Not covered: R32Float is not in store_texel_order, so a non-memoryless
R32Float target lands in guest memory through the CPU converter at eight
bits of precision, and a type-11 surface declared R32Float would get a
resident identity that names BGRA8 over an R32_SFLOAT image, the same
gap RG32Float, RG16Float, R16Float and R8Unorm surfaces already have.

Tests: cargo test --release -p reims-vgpu --no-default-features
--features backend-vulkan,host-window --lib, serially: 2213 passed, 1
failed (the vendor/qemu cursor test, as before). The new test fails
without the change; the old assertion that R32_FLOAT is not renderable
is flipped, and the translate test that used it as the sampled-but-not-
renderable example now uses RG8_UNORM. clippy (toolchain 1.99, Vulkan
arm, -D warnings) reports nothing in the changed lines. No guest was
booted with this change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit bd148d57fde493a5d17a761ae32e59713d02c917)
